{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>Lest it be said: 'YHWH was unable to bring them to the land that He spoke to them.'</b> He said in the section of the spies (Numbers 14:16): 'Because YHWH was unable to bring this people to the land that He swore to them, He slaughtered them in the wilderness' — that is, they will say that when they came and drew near to the land, He saw that there was no power in His hand against those nations, [and so] He slaughtered them in the wilderness. But here he says: 'and in His hatred of them He brought them out to put them to death in the wilderness' — for this hatred was upon them [already] in Egypt, before He brought them out from there. The reason is that in the matter of the Calf they were still near to Egypt, far from the land of Canaan, so they would say that even while they were in Egypt He saw that there was no power in His hand to bring them to the land that He spoke to them in the ears of the Egyptians, and therefore He hated them; and so as not to begin [it] before the eyes of the nations who had it made known to them before their own eyes, He brought them out of Egypt to put them to death in the wilderness, in a place where it would not be known what had happened to them. And this is [the meaning of] 'in evil He brought them out to kill them in the mountains' (Exodus 32:12) — that He devised against them an evil plan before they went out, bringing them out from the midst of the people of Egypt to kill them among the mountains, a place through which no man passes and where no man dwells. The intention in these arguments is that the nations would speak of YHWH, the Elohim of Israel, saying of Him as [they would] of the deities of the lands of the nations, in the manner that is said (Daniel 10:20): 'And now I will return to fight with the prince of Persia.' And I have already mentioned this matter."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:47:25.362435587Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}